  "narrative": "The new panel adds two clear threshold-level associations and one borderline association. For feature_010=1 versus 0, H25 gives a signed positive contrast +0.4232 [0.3268, 0.5195], entirely above the 0.15-unit threshold in the claimed less-negative direction; I accept it. The opposite claim H26 is therefore strongly unsupported. For feature_037=1 versus 0, the positive-oriented H29 is opposite and large, so I reject it, while the already registered reversed negative-oriented claim H30 gives +0.8325 [0.7667, 0.8983], clearly above threshold; I accept H30 as a stronger-dependency association. These two findings are large enough that multiplicity is unlikely to explain them, although they remain dataset-specific associations rather than causal effects.\n\nFor feature_063=1 versus 0, the negative-oriented H44 gives +0.2268 [0.1307, 0.3229]. The point estimate exceeds threshold, but the lower confidence bound is slightly below threshold, so the discovery evidence is compatible with, but not decisive for, a meaningful threshold-level stronger-dependency association. Given this borderline interval and the number of exploratory contrasts, I keep H44 unresolved and request independent validation. This is the one new validation request this iteration.\n\nMost other requested predictors are null or subthreshold in both directions: feature_048, feature_023, feature_060, feature_033, feature_052 level_001 versus level_003, and feature_061 level_001 versus level_002. For feature_046 level_002 versus level_001, H64 was opposite to the registered negative claim, and the corresponding positive raw contrast is below threshold, so no reversed threshold claim is warranted. The feature_002 interaction with feature_046 level_001 is small and imprecise, so H57 is rejected. The low-severity feature_003 contrast H61 is below threshold and imprecise; this closes the feature_003 low-severity threshold line and leaves feature_003 as a collection of subthreshold or unresolved findings rather than an accepted threshold-level predictor.\n\nI registered conditional robustness analyses for feature_010, feature_037, and feature_002 to determine whether these predictors are independent signals, partially confounded, or overlapping with the already accepted feature_002 result. These follow-ups do not alter current acceptance; they aim to clarify whether each large effect persists when another measured predictor is held at a fixed level.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted within-dataset threshold claims: H47 feature_002=1 vs 0 positive/less-negative +0.8315 [0.7658,0.8972]; H25 feature_010=1 vs 0 positive/less-negative +0.4232 [0.3268,0.5195]; H30 feature_037=1 vs 0 negative/stronger-dependency +0.8325 [0.7667,0.8983]. H30 is the accepted reversed form of the positive-oriented H29, which is rejected. Feature_002 robustness previously accepted within feature_003 and severity/log-PFS strata.\n\nH44 feature_063=1 vs 0 negative/stronger-dependency is borderline: signed +0.2268 [0.1307,0.3229], point above threshold but lower bound below 0.15. Independent validation requested for H44; do not accept until validation is assessed. Validation remaining after request: 7.\n\nNull/subthreshold new predictors: feature_048, feature_023, feature_060, feature_033, feature_052 level_001 vs level_003, feature_061 level_001 vs level_002, and feature_046 level_002 vs level_001. H57 feature_002 interaction with feature_046 level_001 is null. H61 feature_003 low-severity contrast is subthreshold and closes the low-severity feature_003 threshold pursuit; other feature_003 conditional/global claims remain unresolved subthreshold findings and low priority. Feature_031 remains subthreshold; H23/H62 deferred, H63 rejected.\n\nNewly registered follow-up panel tests conditional persistence of feature_010 within feature_037 and feature_002 strata, feature_037 within feature_010 and feature_002 strata, and feature_002 within feature_010 and feature_037 strata. Purpose: distinguish independent associations from confounding/collinearity among the largest measured binary predictors. Acceptance criteria remain the same: accept only when signed point exceeds 0.15 with uncertainty compatible with a threshold-level effect in the claimed direction; reject opposite or clearly subthreshold results; keep unresolved when uncertainty genuinely prevents a threshold conclusion. All conclusions are dataset-specific associations, not causal or biological-mechanistic claims.",
