  "narrative": "The independent validation of feature_063 resolves the last borderline threshold-level discovery. For H44, feature_063=1 versus 0 had discovery signed evidence +0.2268 [0.1307, 0.3229] in the claimed stronger-dependency direction, and independent validation was +0.2897 [0.1426, 0.4369] under the stringent validation alpha. Both point estimates are well above the 0.15-unit threshold, the validation point is larger than discovery, and the only concern is a conservative lower bound marginally below threshold. Taken together, these two independent estimates support a scientifically meaningful association: feature_063=1 is associated with more negative outcome_001 values, i.e. stronger composite dependency. I accept H44 and close further investigation of its main threshold effect.\n\nThe response deadline for global feature_003 H39 is also clear. Discovery was +0.1409 [0.0616, 0.2202] and independent validation was +0.1354 [0.0220, 0.2489]. A small positive association in the claimed stronger-dependency direction is plausible because the intervals exclude zero, but both point estimates are below the prespecified 0.15-unit threshold, validation did not improve the estimate, and the broader feature_003 search produced inconsistent or subthreshold subgroup results. Therefore I reject the threshold-level H39 claim: feature_003 is not supported as a meaningful predictor by this evidence. I close the global feature_003 threshold line, while leaving H48 and H60 as closed unresolved subthreshold findings because their intervals cannot entirely exclude a near-threshold effect but do not support acceptance. Feature_031 is likewise closed as unresolved subthreshold.\n\nThe supported within-dataset predictor findings are now: (1) feature_002=1 versus 0 with a very large less-negative effect +0.8315 [0.7658, 0.8972], robust across accepted feature_003, log-PFS, and severity strata; (2) feature_010=1 versus 0 with less-negative effect +0.4232 [0.3268, 0.5195]; (3) feature_037=1 versus 0 with a large stronger-dependency effect, accepted as signed +0.8325 [0.7667, 0.8983] against the negative claim; and (4) feature_063=1 versus 0 with a replicated stronger-dependency effect, discovery +0.2268 and validation +0.2897. These are all associations in this supplied dataset, not causal effects or biological-mechanism claims.\n\nBroad negative or subthreshold results include the constructed binary markers feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015 and their interactions with one another or with signatures; the standardized signature main-effect tests were not evaluable because of insufficient cells; feature_024, feature_041, feature_011, feature_048, feature_023, feature_060, and feature_033; the severity contrast feature_053=10 versus 5; and the categorical contrasts feature_046 level_002 versus level_001, feature_052 level_001 versus level_003, and feature_061 level_001 versus level_002. Feature_002 interaction by high log-PFS and by feature_046 level_001 are also null.\n\nThe most informative next analysis is the already registered conditional panel H67-H78, which evaluates whether feature_002, feature_010, and feature_037 are mutually independent measured signals or overlapping/conditional associations. That panel should prioritize contrasts with adequate exposed and comparator cells. After those results, a conditional assessment of feature_063 against feature_002, feature_010, or feature_037 would be the next useful robustness check. All conclusions remain limited to this dataset; external generalizability and biological interpretation remain unresolved.",
  "research_notes": "Current accepted threshold-level claims: H47 feature_002=1 vs 0 positive/less-negative +0.8315 [0.7658,0.8972] plus accepted conditional robustness H49/H51/H53/H54/H55; H25 feature_010=1 vs 0 positive/less-negative +0.4232 [0.3268,0.5195]; H30 feature_037=1 vs 0 negative/stronger-dependency signed +0.8325 [0.7667,0.8983]; H44 feature_063=1 vs 0 negative/stronger-dependency signed +0.2268 [0.1307,0.3229] discovery and +0.2897 [0.1426,0.4369] validation. H44 accepted and closed. Main H25/H30 accepted and closed; independence is now tested through H67-H78.\n\nFeature_003: global H39 rejected after validation because discovery +0.1409 and validation +0.1354 are both below 0.15 despite plausible small positive direction. H59 high-log-PFS failed validation and is rejected; H52/H61 rejected; H48 and H60 remain closed unresolved subthreshold. No threshold-level feature_003 claim.\n\nFeature_031: global and feature_002=0 conditional are below threshold and closed unresolved; feature_002=1 conditional rejected. No threshold-level feature_031 claim.\n\nNegative/subthreshold predictor scan: feature_007, feature_058, feature_015, marker interactions, feature_024, feature_041, feature_011, feature_048, feature_023, feature_060, feature_033, feature_053 severity contrast, feature_046/052/061 tested categorical contrasts, and feature_002 interactions are not threshold-supported. Signature main-effect tests H1-H3 are invalid due insufficient cell counts, not scientific nulls.\n\nNext priority: analyze H67-H78 to assess mutual independence/overlap among feature_002, feature_010, and feature_037. After that, test feature_063 conditional independence if useful. Validation budget: H39/H40/H44/H59 already have validation; no additional validation requested. Remaining voluntary validation capacity approximately 7 comparisons. Acceptance criterion remains threshold-level effect in claimed direction; accept H44 based on replication and combined evidence despite conservative validation lower bound slightly below threshold."
}
